  "historical_output_text": " How and where to sow seed indoors:\n\nFirst find or create containers, preferably small plastic boxes. Choose seeds suited your local conditions and climate zone for best chance success.\nSecond place seed in moist pot soil or a growing substrate mix that retains enough damp without puddlying, enough oxygen, no weeds.\nThen put container somewhere in bright sunlight for at home growing.\nKeep seed moist by regularly water from below to not drown or from the soil to not blow off.\nAs roots develop from a couple days or less you’ll need some way, a tray of small rocks and plastic cover for greenhouse conditions if not in the bright sunshine of an indoor room.\n\n",
